From 092f5d51d0844f7cf282ca115a81fccdde9fafad Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Han <danielhanchen@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 23:16:25 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] ggml : rope_pe_permute with the per-head RMS norm folded in

ggml_rope_pe_permute_rms(a, pe, n_rot, scale, type, eps) is ggml_rope_pe_permute of
ggml_rms_norm(a, eps) without a weight. CPU uses rms_norm's arithmetic (double sum,
1/sqrtf, vec scale); CUDA normalises each head row with the block size and block
reduction rms_norm_f32_cuda's small-row path uses for that row length, so both match
the two-op chain bit for bit. CUDA supports it for head_dim <= 128 when that small-row
path is active (not HIP/MUSA, GGML_CUDA_NORM_SMALL_ROWS not 0); elsewhere the op is
reported unsupported and callers keep the separate norm. test-backend-ops cases added.
---
 include/ggml.h             |  12 ++++
 src/ggml-cpu/ops.cpp       |  17 +++++-
 src/ggml-cuda/rope-pe.cu   | 120 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 src/ggml.c                 |  15 +++++
 tests/test-backend-ops.cpp |  15 +++--
 5 files changed, 174 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

